course: dictionary
lesson: 2745
title: Disagree and agree politely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disagree is a verb. It means to have a different opinion from someone else, or to not match. «I disagree with you about the ending» tells us the speaker thinks differently. «The two answers disagree» means the answers do not match.
explain: Disagree changes its form: disagrees, disagreed, disagreeing. Look at the start of the word. Dis- turns agree into its opposite. You can disagree with a person, or disagree about a thing.
explain: Disagreeing is fine when you do it politely and give a reason. Say «I disagree, because…» and then explain your idea. Being rude or unkind is not the same as disagreeing.
fact: Disagree means to have a different opinion from someone else.
fact: The beginning dis- often means "not" or "the opposite of", so disagree is the opposite of agree.
fact: If two answers disagree, they do not match. In maths, that means someone has made a mistake, so check the working.
fact: Food that disagrees with you makes you feel sick.
fact: Useful phrases: disagree with, disagree about, agree to disagree, strongly disagree.
exercise: Danylo says, «Anyone who disagrees is an enemy.» What does disagrees mean here? | *To have a different opinion from someone else | To agree and say yes to everything | To shout very loudly | To leave the room quietly
exercise: «The two answers disagree.» In maths, what does this tell you? | Both answers are right | *The answers do not match, so check the working | Someone has won the game | The answers are exactly the same
exercise: Which is the polite way to disagree? | Say, «You are wrong and silly.» | Laugh and walk away without speaking | Shout the answer loudly | *Say, «I disagree, because I think the story ends sadly.»
test: Scientists often ___ about ideas, so they test them to find out the truth. Which word fits the gap? | disgust | discover | *disagree | disappear
test: Which phrase means two people accept that they will not agree? | strongly agree | *agree to disagree | disagree with the sun
exam: Jayden says, «Saying I disagree is always rude.» What is the best answer? | Yes, but only in maths lessons | Yes, you must never disagree with anyone | *No, you can disagree politely and give a reason | No, disagree means to agree
